# Prime: rules

- `slopvac rules --format md` prints each rule in full for you to read. `--format json` prints data.
- `--kind`, `--category` and `--genre` select rules. The list keeps rules that match every filter you give.
- `--include-excluded` keeps rules that the config turns off.
- `slopvac explain <rule_id> --format md` prints the fix, the examples and the named exceptions of one rule.
- Suppress a finding only with a named exception of its rule. Never suppress to hide a defect in prose you wrote.
- Rule ids carry a pack namespace.
{% if level == "full" %}
- Judgement rules need a reader: `slopvac rules --kind judgement --format md`.
{% endif %}
